<title>FRANCE: EU gives wheat export help for Sub-Saharan Africa.</title>
<headline>EU gives wheat export help for Sub-Saharan Africa.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday set set up a special export refund of 12 Ecus per tonne for soft wheat being exported to a group of poor, mainly Sub-Saharan African countries, European grain officials said.</p>
<p>The refund of 12 Ecus will apply to wheat exports up until December 31, they said.</p>
<p>From January 1 until June 30, 1996, a positive corrective of seven Ecus per tonne will be added to the refund, increasing its value to 19 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>The officials declined to name the countries which would benefit but stressed only African nations were involved.</p>
</text>
